<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Di Yi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Di Yi was the penultimate king of the Shang dynasty and father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/di-xin">Di Xin</a>, the last Shang king. Oracle-bone inscriptions of his reign show a strict, regular schedule of sacrifices to the royal ancestors and campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renfang">Renfang</a>, peoples to the east of the Shang heartland. He ruled from the capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yinxu">Yinxu</a> near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anyang">Anyang</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/di-yi.jpg" alt="Di Yi" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 氏子 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B8%B6%E5%88%BB%E8%BE%AD%E8%81%96%E6%B0%B4%E7%89%9B%E9%A0%AD%E9%AA%A8%EF%BC%88%E7%94%B23939%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
